:null,"donor_test":"not significant","donor_padj":0.865534,"donor_log2fc":0.155144,"donor_lfcse":0.164043,"donor_log2fc_shrunk":0.00631719}],"modules":[],"degas_bulk_de":false,"drug_target":false}},"description":[{"gene_id":"ENSG00000184967","entrez_id":["79050"],"uniprot":["Q9BVI4"],"ncbi_summary":"Enables RNA binding activity. Predicted to be involved in rRNA processing. Located in nucleolus and nucleoplasm. [provided by Alliance of Genome Resources, Apr 2022]","ncbi_source":"NCBI Gene summary (RefSeq), via MyGene.info","uniprot_function":[{"accession":"Q9BVI4","text":"Part of the small subunit (SSU) processome, first precursor of the small eukaryotic ribosomal subunit (PubMed:34516797). During the assembly of the SSU processome in the nucleolus, many ribosome biogenesis factors, an RNA chaperone and ribosomal proteins associate with the nascent pre-rRNA and work in concert to generate RNA folding, modifications, rearrangements and cleavage as well as targeted degradation of pre-ribosomal RNA by the RNA exosome (PubMed:34516797). Required for the translation of mRNAs related to activation of regulatory and conventional T cells but is not essential for global translation in regulatory T cells (By similarity). Ensures correct nucleolar localization of small ribosomal subunit processome member EMG1 as part of a complex with NOP14 and UTP14A (PubMed:27798105). Blocks TLR4 endocytosis, causing inhibition of the TICAM1/TRIF signaling pathway (By similarity). This leads to reduced production of inflammatory cytokines which ameliorates local and systemic inflammation and influences insulin sensitivity (By similarity). Inhibits SIRT1-mediated deacetylation of TP53/p53 (PubMed:36030331). Required during early embryogenesis to ensure blastocyst formation (By similarity)."}],"uniprot_source":"UniProtKB/Swiss-Prot Function, release 2026_04","retrieved":"2026-10-21"}],"structures":[],"alphafold_accessions":[]}